<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE score-partwise PUBLIC "-//Recordare//DTD MusicXML 4.0 Partwise//EN" "http://www.musicxml.org/dtds/partwise.dtd">
<!--
  A score written to be a picture of engraved notation.

  The two fixtures beside this one are whole notes: they photograph the import
  summary's text, which is what they exist for, and they photograph nothing a
  renderer does. This one is the input to a reference image of a staff, so every
  construct the first engraving pass draws appears in it exactly once and
  nothing else does:

    bar 1  key signature of two sharps, 4/4, a forward repeat, a tempo mark,
           lyrics, a note inside the key needing no accidental, and a pair of
           eighths sharing one beat, which beam
    bar 2  an accidental outside the key, the same accidental not repeated, a
           natural cancelling it, and a rest
    bar 3  a grace note, a dotted quarter, two eighths each alone in a beat and
           so flagged, a pair of sixteenths sharing a beat and so beamed with a
           second beam, and a backward repeat
    bars 4-5  a tie across a barline, whose second note carries no accidental
    bar 6  a clef change, and the notes after it on the new staff
    bar 7  a chord, and a chord holding two notes a second apart
    bar 8  a whole note and the final barline

  Hand-written for this repository, like the two beside it, and made only of
  constructs the importer fully supports -- so it imports with no diagnostics
  and the picture is of the renderer rather than of a report.

  **There is deliberately no dynamic marking in it**, even though the renderer
  draws one and #32 asks for "basic dynamics". A <dynamics><mf/></dynamics> is
  read correctly by the importer and *also* reported by it as an element it does
  not read: the marking names live in `isDynamicMarking` and not in
  `knownElements`, so the recursive unrecognised-element walk counts every one
  of them. Putting a dynamic here would make this file import with a diagnostic
  and make the picture say the file was not fully read. The renderer's handling
  of dynamics is covered by ScoreLayoutEngineTests instead, which builds a
  `score::Direction` directly. The importer defect is recorded in
  docs/development/architecture/score-model-findings.md.

  Divisions are 4, so a quarter note is 4 and a bar of 4/4 is 16.
-->
